<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Ellerine year shr up, warns on crime.</title>
<headline>Ellerine year shr up, warns on crime.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Aug 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     176.9	 vs 132.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 58.8	  vs 44.0</p>
<p>    Earned for shareholders 130.20    vs 95.61</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   202.03	vs 146.77</p>
<p>    Tax			 71.84	 vs 50.97</p>
<p>    Interest		  7.24 gain   vs 2.77 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,101.80    vs 862.95</p>
<p>Full name : Ellerine Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Div payable November 20</p>
<p>on register October 25</p>
<p>NOTE - Furniture and retail group Ellerine said the failure of government to build more housing and to stimulate the economy had been disappointing.</p>
<p>It added that the group's performance in the coming year would depend largely on the level of real growth in the economy. &quot;Spiralling violence and crime remain a serious cause for concern,&quot; the group added.</p>
<p>But Ellerine said that, given no deterioration in the country's economic situation, it is still well placed to deliver solid earnings growth.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
